**6. MVP Risk Register**

The following risks are identified as having the highest potential to
affect the v1.0 launch timeline, quality, or adoption. Each risk
includes a mitigation strategy.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Risk**              **Likelihood**   **Impact**   **Mitigation**
  --------------------- ---------------- ------------ --------------------------------------
  QuickBooks            Medium           High         Begin QBO integration in Sprint 3 ---
  integration                                         parallel track with project features.
  complexity delays                                   Allocate dedicated engineer.
  launch                                              

  Mobile offline sync   Medium           High         Design conflict resolution rules in
  introduces data                                     data model before development begins.
  conflicts                                           Test extensively with simulated
                                                      connectivity loss.

  Multi-tenant          Low              Critical     Security audit at Sprint 2 completion.
  row-level security                                  Penetration test before beta.
  has edge case leaks                                 Automated tenant isolation tests in CI
                                                      pipeline.

  Trade module scope    Medium           Medium       Detailed spec for both modules
  underestimated for                                  complete before Sprint 3. Buffer 20%
  Electrical/Plumbing                                 in estimates for trade module work.

  Beta customers find   Medium           High         Field usability testing at Sprint 7
  core UX confusing for                               with actual contractors. Mobile-first
  field use                                           design review at each sprint.

  Onboarding drop-off   Medium           Medium       In-app onboarding wizard, email drip
  --- tenants sign up                                 campaign, optional concierge
  but don\'t activate                                 onboarding call for early customers.

  DocuSign e-signature  Low              Medium       Test full change order workflow
  adds friction to                                    end-to-end in beta. Offer native
  change order flow                                   signature fallback if needed.

  Launch timeline slips Medium           Medium       Define hard scope freeze at Month 4.
  beyond 9 months                                     Any new requests after scope freeze go
                                                      to v1.1 backlog --- no exceptions.
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**7. Definition of Done --- v1.0**

v1.0 is complete and ready for public launch when ALL of the following
conditions are met:

**Product Completeness**

-   All features marked v1.0 --- SHIP in this document are implemented
    and passing QA

-   All 3 trade modules (GC, Electrical, Plumbing) fully functional with
    phase gates and checklists

-   iOS and Android apps submitted and approved in App Store and Google
    Play

-   Offline mode tested and verified across iOS and Android on simulated
    poor connectivity

-   Client portal functional and tested with real client user accounts

-   Free subcontractor portal functional and tested

**Integrations**

-   QuickBooks Online bi-directional sync verified with live QBO
    accounts in beta

-   Stripe billing --- subscription creation, upgrade, downgrade,
    cancellation, and failed payment handling all verified

-   DocuSign e-signature flow tested end-to-end for change orders and
    contracts

-   All notification pathways (email via SendGrid, SMS via Twilio, push
    via mobile) verified

**Security & Infrastructure**

-   Tenant isolation penetration test passed --- no cross-tenant data
    access possible

-   All data in transit encrypted via TLS 1.3

-   All data at rest encrypted via AES-256

-   MFA implementation tested

-   99.9% uptime infrastructure configured with monitoring and alerting
    live

-   Automated daily backups verified with successful restore test

**Performance**

-   Page load time under 2 seconds on standard broadband for all primary
    screens

-   Mobile app launches under 3 seconds cold start on mid-range devices

-   Plan viewer loads a 50MB plan set in under 5 seconds

-   Load tested to 200 concurrent users without degradation

**Business Readiness**

-   Self-serve signup flow tested end-to-end --- new tenant to first
    project in under 10 minutes

-   Subscription billing tested --- all tiers, monthly and annual,
    upgrade and downgrade

-   Support system live --- ticketing, knowledge base, onboarding
    documentation

-   Super admin console operational --- tenant management, billing
    visibility, feature flags

-   Beta feedback addressed --- all P1 and P2 bugs resolved, P3 bugs
    documented in backlog

-   Privacy policy, terms of service, and data processing agreement
    published

